        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport, Cheyenne Regional Airport, downtown Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming\n- Systems: IATA, ICAO, FAA LID\n- Concepts: civil-military airports, international airports, public use airports\n\nFacts:\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is also known as Wold–Chamberlain Field.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport has the codes IATA MSP, ICAO KMSP, and FAA LID MSP.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is a joint civil-military public use international airport.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport is also known as Jerry Olson Field.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport has the codes IATA CYS, ICAO KCYS, and FAA LID CYS.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport is a civil-military airport located one mile north of downtown Cheyenne in Laramie County, Wyoming.",
